Tell a frontend with no window an MXP frame's tabs, and let it bring one forward

An internal MXP frame given a TITLE, not FLOATING and at least 50 pixels tall (or sized in characters) has a tab
header (TMxpFrameManager::layoutInternalFrame's showHeader): TMxpFrameWidgets draws it with a QTabWidget whose first
page is the frame's own console and whose other pages are the DOCK frames opened into it with Align="client", each
tab showing the frame's TITLE, or its name. A player clicks a tab to bring its page forward; no script can.
THeadlessSession told only, in a page's shown, whether it was the one in front, so an app could neither draw the tabs
nor let the player switch them.

- TNullMxpFrameFrontend keeps each page's title, as the QTabWidget does, and gains tabs(), headerOf() and
  selectPage(), which does what QTabWidget::setCurrentIndex() does: the page comes forward at the size the header
  gives the page in front, and the frames whose shown changes are reported.
- THeadlessSession::ScriptWindow carries a header frame's frameTabs (each page's frame name and title, and the index
  of the one in front), so a new title or front page names the frame in scriptWindowsChanged. A page, and a frame
  without a header, has none.
- THeadlessSession::selectFrameTab(page) is the player's click on a tab. It raises no event, as the click raises
  none in the GUI; it is true, changing nothing, for the page already in front, and false, with errorString(), for a
  name that is no page of a header, for a header whose page in front is not shown (inside a hidden EXTERNAL frame)
  and where runLua() is refused.
- docs/headless.md describes both, and drops the tab header from "What still needs a window".

Tested in HeadlessSessionWindowTextTest (the titles, the page in front, bringing one forward and back, the refusals,
a header inside a hidden EXTERNAL frame, and closing the page in front). The desktop is unchanged.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.
Upstream: not opened yet

